@startuml UC-39 Remove Student - Sequence Diagram (icon)
skinparam defaultFontName "Segoe UI"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #000000
skinparam DatabaseBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #000000
skinparam ArrowColor #000000
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam maxMessageSize 280
title 2.12.2.9 UC-39 Remove Student — Sequence Diagram

actor Teacher
boundary ":AddStudentPage" as UI
control ":ClassController" as CTL
control ":ClassEnrollmentService" as SVC
boundary ":ClassMemberRepository" as MEM
database DB

autonumber
Teacher ->> UI : Open the actions of an enrolled student in the Class Members list of an owned ACTIVE class and select "Remove"
activate UI
UI ->> UI : openRemoveDialog(member)
UI -->> Teacher : Show the removal confirmation popup with an optional reason (MSG09)

opt teacher cancels the removal
  Teacher ->> UI : Click "Cancel"
  UI -->> Teacher : Close the popup and leave the enrollment unchanged
end

Teacher ->> UI : Enter an optional reason and click "Remove from class" to confirm
UI ->> UI : handleRemoveStudent()
UI ->> CTL : DELETE /api/classes/{id}/members/{studentId}
activate CTL
CTL ->> SVC : removeStudent(classId, studentId, reason)
activate SVC
SVC ->> SVC : resolve the class and accept only an owned class that is still ACTIVE
SVC ->> MEM : findAnyByClassIdAndStudentId(classId, studentId)
activate MEM
MEM ->> DB : SELECT * FROM class_members WHERE class_id = ? AND student_id = ?
activate DB
DB -->> MEM : row / none
deactivate DB
MEM -->> SVC : ClassMember
deactivate MEM
SVC ->> SVC : accept only a membership that is still ENROLLED

alt class is not owned or is INACTIVE, or the student is no longer enrolled
  SVC -->> CTL : ForbiddenOperationException / ResourceNotFoundException
  CTL -->> UI : HTTP 403 / 404
  UI -->> Teacher : Show MSG23 or the not-enrolled message and refresh the Class Members list

else the teacher owns an ACTIVE class and the student is still enrolled
  SVC ->> MEM : save(ClassMember with status REMOVED, the remover and the reason)
  activate MEM
  MEM ->> DB : UPDATE class_members SET status = 'REMOVED', removal columns WHERE id = ?
  activate DB
  DB -->> MEM : Saved
  deactivate DB
  MEM -->> SVC : ClassMember
  deactivate MEM
  SVC -->> CTL : RemoveResult
  CTL -->> UI : HTTP 200 + RemoveStudentResponse
  UI ->> UI : loadMembers(id)
  UI -->> Teacher : Show the successful removal message and the refreshed list; the student account and submission rows stay preserved
end
deactivate SVC
deactivate CTL
deactivate UI
@enduml
